{"duration_api_ms":3271,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f0a3703a-ffae-4680-956e-9cb3e11f72f7","total_cost_usd":0.0007570999999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":749,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":412},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":749,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1051},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1594,"outputTokens":775,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1051,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0007570999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":412,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1051,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Shortfall when assets are small:** The sponsor (adviser) bears it. Under a unitary fee, the sponsor receives a fixed percentage of fund assets and pays operating expenses from it. As assets shrink, fee income falls but expense obligations don't, so the sponsor's margin absorbs the gap. Shareholders keep the fixed expense ratio, though they still bear trading costs and excluded expenses.\n\n**If the sponsor fails to pay:** The fund remains liable. Service providers (custodians, auditors, transfer agents, administrators) contract with the trust and can look to fund assets. Those amounts reduce NAV, so shareholders bear them and can then pursue the sponsor under the agreement. The board would typically act to protect the fund by replacing the sponsor, terminating the arrangement, or liquidating.\n\nThis reflects general structure through my knowledge cutoff. Expense caps, reimbursement, and waiver terms vary by fund, so verify them against the prospectus and sponsor agreement.","ttft_ms":1827,"type":"result","duration_ms":2763,"uuid":"1ae7afae-0470-45ef-bff8-606f1625eac8","ttft_stream_ms":417,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":417,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
